# Config for the file-upload skill.
#
# Install on a new host:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/i-upload
#   cp config.example ~/.config/i-upload/config
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/i-upload/config
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/i-upload/config     # paste the key below
#
# Sourced as a shell fragment. Env vars of the same name take precedence,
# so `UPLOAD_KEY=... upload.sh file.png` works without a config file at all.

# Required. The AUTH_KEY secret of the deployed worker — from Cloudflare
# (`wrangler secret list` shows only that it exists, not its value), or from
# whatever you passed to `wrangler secret put AUTH_KEY`. Never commit this.
UPLOAD_KEY=

# Optional. Override only when pointing at a second deployment or a local
# `wrangler dev` instance (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8787).
#UPLOAD_ENDPOINT=https://i.mia.cx

# Requires: bash, curl, jq, file (all preinstalled on macOS except jq —
# `brew install jq`).
